id=a52sxq_ksu_metamodule
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: KernelSU metamodule by default (meta-overlayfs 1.3.1-k4.1)
author=kusti420
description=Metamodule-era KernelSU (ksud 4.x, here ReSukiSU/BakaSU 4.2.0) no longer mounts module files itself: without a metamodule (/data/adb/metamodule) modules install but their system/ vendor/ files never appear, so testers needed Mountify. The ROM ships the official reference metamodule meta-overlayfs 1.3.1 (KernelSU Developers, GPL-3.0, KernelSU-Modules-Repo release) as its build 1.3.1-k4.1 (three scripts changed, binaries unmodified, sha256 pinned, PROVENANCE.txt, meta-overlayfs-k4/K4_CHANGES.txt: Adreno GPU driver modules are never mounted by it but imported by the GPU driver selector with the right SELinux labels and a trial boot - the unmodified build mounted them with label vendor_file and SurfaceFlinger bootlooped - plus image label and cleanup fixes) in /system/etc/k4/ksu and, on boot_completed, installs it through ksud's own installer (ksud module install) when KernelSU is active, Magisk is not, no metamodule is installed or pending, and the user did not opt out. An installed unmodified meta-overlayfs 1.3.1 (versionCode 13100) is updated to this build in place, and a fresh install is completed at once: nothing is left pending, since ksud refuses every module install while a metamodule is pending until a reboot (TEE Simulator could not be installed on the first boot of 9.3.83). It is mounted by ksud from the next boot on (the first boot after flashing needs one extra reboot). Opt-out: uninstall the metamodule in the KernelSU manager (any metamodule that was seen and is then gone writes /data/adb/.k4_metamodule_optout, so switching metamodules is never raced), or setprop persist.sys.k4.ksu_metamodule 0 (adb shell); 1 re-arms it once. An existing metamodule (Mountify, magic mount, ...) or other module is never touched. Without KernelSU only a confined check runs (domain k4ksumeta, it can only stat /data/adb/ksud, a file only KernelSU's policy lets it see); the install runs in KernelSU's own domain. Result in sys.k4.ksu_meta, log /data/adb/.k4_metamodule.log. Modules installed before the metamodule (none yet, or another metamodule such as Mountify) are copied into meta-overlayfs's modules.img on boot_completed the way its metainstall.sh would have done it (same conditions and labels; disabled, skip_mount and Adreno GPU driver modules are left out, a module already in the image is never touched), so they are mounted from the next boot on without a reinstall (sys.k4.ksu_meta_import).
